When you encounter a ghost level in which an angry shopkeeper killed your own
character, the shopkeeper is still angry at you, unless you have been
polymorphed, felt like a new man, and changed your name. Thus the shopkeeper
goes by your name, not your appearance. How does he know your name? Even if you
have been polymorphed into a different monster, as long as your name's the
same, the shopkeeper is angry at you. Perhaps shopkeepers should ask for
identification, at least after they have been robbed?

If you polymorph a Mimic, you still `cannot escape' the new monster.

